# Gmail API Configuration (OAuth 2.0 - Recommended)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Create a Google Cloud Project at https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Enable the Gmail API (APIs & Services > Enable APIs and Services > Gmail API)
# 3. Configure OAuth Consent Screen (External or Internal) and add scope:
#    https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send
# 4. Create Credentials > OAuth client ID (Desktop App or Web Application)
# 5. Obtain Client ID, Client Secret, and Refresh Token
GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=your_oauth_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=your_oauth_client_secret
GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN=your_oauth_refresh_token
GMAIL_SENDER_EMAIL=your_email@gmail.com

# Alternative Quick Option: Gmail App Password (SMTP)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# If you don't have OAuth refresh tokens ready yet, you can generate an App Password:
# 1. Go to Google Account > Security > 2-Step Verification
# 2. At the bottom, click 'App passwords'
# 3. Generate a password for 'Mail'
# 4. Fill in:
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=your_16_digit_app_password
